    "updated_at": "2017-08-22T20:10:25Z",
    "body": "thanks.  to test my understanding, is this correct? \r\n> Structs differ from [maps](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-map) and [Records](https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#idl-record) in that a struct has a well-defined and immutable set of keys.\r\n\r\n..? if so, perhaps it ought to be added to [infra's Structs section](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#structs) ?\r\n\r\nIt seems there is no present way to formally declare something of type `struct` using WebIDL ?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
