    "created_at": "2022-05-03T07:33:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-05-03T07:33:57Z",
    "body": "Well, for maps the names are essentially values. For structs the names are immutable identifiers. That is a bit different at least and would visually show they are different, albeit very subtly.\r\n\r\nAlso, maps and IDL records are conceptually very much the same thing. Just like lists and IDL sequences. Maps and structs are not.",
